# Natural: the scale follows the light (Yo by day, Min'yo from golden hour through the night: a scene's notes all sound
# well over its chords), and every third dawn the key may move a fourth or fifth, never more than a fifth from the
# instrument's; the instrument's own key and scale are untouched, and back in the engine on leaving
# (ZEN-1 boots into the scene: Sakura, Natural, a morning)
wait 800
expect scalecur 1
expect par1 0
# fifteen dawns at once: five chances for the key to move
dawns 15
wait 20000
expect changes >1
expect keyoff >-701
expect keyoff <701
expect par0 4
expect par1 0
shot drifted.png
# the night: Min'yo (taken when the notes rest, within a minute anyway)
dayat 0.7
wait 61000
expect scalecur 2
# the instrument: its key and scale, as saved
press HOME
wait 800
release HOME
wait 200
expect mode 0
expect par1 0
expect key1cents -2320
